{title: Who You Say I Am}
{song_number: 133}
{language: en}
{artist: Reuben Morgan and Ben Fielding}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Who am I, that the highest King would [Em]welcome [D]me?
[G]I was lost, but He brought me in. Oh, His [Em]love for [D]me!
[C]Oh, His [Em]love for [D]me!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Free at last, He has ransomed me, His [Em]grace runs [D]deep.
[G]While I was a slave to sin, Jesus [Em]died for [D]me.
[C]Yes, He [Em]died for [D]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Who the Son sets free, oh, is [D]free indeed.
I'm a [Em]child of [D]God, yes, [C]I am.
[G]In my Father's house there's a [D]place for me.
I'm a [Em]child of [D]God, yes, [C]I am, [G]I am.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Em]I am chosen, not for[D/F#]saken.
I [G]am who You say I am.
[C]You are [Em]for me, not a[D/F#]gainst me.
I [G]am who You say I am.
{end_of_bridge}

{comment: Repeat bridge; ending: Oh, I am who You say I am. Yes, I am who You say I am.}
